    <content:encoded>[caption id="attachment_4299" align="aligncenter" width="509"]&lt;img class="  wp-image-4299 aligncenter" src="https://flyingsummers.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/08/img_0029.jpg" alt="img_0029.jpg" width="509" height="382" /&gt; Ilya and his 9 and 7 year olds[/caption]

If you are here to learn about flying your DA40 Diamondstar (or similarly-sized and equipped airplane) &lt;a href="https://flyingsummers.com/crossing-the-country/"&gt;across the country&lt;/a&gt;, you might be a little disappointed since &lt;a href="https://flyingsummers.com/n972rd/"&gt;we switched planes&lt;/a&gt;. But my friend Ilya has done it, and &lt;a href="https://loggingflight.com/2018/08/12/skytrip-to-toronto/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;documented his experience&lt;/a&gt;, and I have a feeling that if you keep an eye on &lt;a href="https://loggingflight.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;his blog&lt;/a&gt; you will be learning more about those adventures.

&lt;!--more--&gt;

(I was surprised at the parallels of our experiences and the fact that he was starting his DA40 flying adventures when his boys were 9 and 7, just like Rudy and Dexter were when we started flying in N971RD. There's even a photo and video somewhere of Dexter playing with that same FBO cat in Flagstaff.)</content:encoded>
